{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 72, :comments ["<b>Pagiel son of Ochran.</b> It alludes, according to their words (Sifrei Devarim 355), that Asher reported to his brothers the deed of Reuben, and they reprimanded him; and when Reuben confessed, they accepted the words of Asher and drew him near — and this is the expression <b>pag'i El</b>, meaning, his brothers encountered him after they had investigated him." "<b>Further,</b> it intends, along the lines of the verse ״בָּרוּךְ מִבָּנִים אָשֵׁר״ (Deuteronomy 33:24). And our Sages of blessed memory said there, and this is their language: there is none among all the tribes who was blessed with children like Asher, end quote. And we find that the blessing of children surrounds the dwelling of holiness, and this is your sign: the Ark of the Torah that lodged in the house of Oved-Edom the Gittite, etc. (Berakhot 63:), and this is the expression <b>pag'i El</b> — that El encountered him, for from this he was blessed with children. And his being called <b>son of Ochran</b> alludes to the removal of virgin blood from their daughters, as they of blessed memory said (Tanna DeBei Eliyahu Rabbah, chapter 9) that they had no virgin blood."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:47.196312335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}